    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it feels like you're still leaning pretty heavily towards the targeted side, though. you mention it's \"more pragmatic,\" but if we look at the automation and AI disruptions coming, isn't the argument essentially that targeted programs will never be fast or broad enough to catch everyone? in that context, wouldn't you say UBI is actually the more logically sound, inevitable solution for stability rather than just a theoretical alternative?",
